"><a data-pjax=3D"true" title=3D"Migrate the default development branch to =
the Rust engine (#2279)

Replace the tree wholesale with the Rust implementation of FalkorDB. This
branch becomes the development line for 6.0 and later; the C engine
continues on `master` with its own CI, releases and maintenance.

The tree of this commit is byte-identical to `main-rs`, the branch carrying
the Rust engine's full 2,873-commit history. That history is deliberately
NOT an ancestor here: this commit has a single parent on `master`'s
lineage, so `git log main` stays linear -- `master`'s history followed by
one migration commit.

Consequence: `main-rs` is the only ref reaching the Rust history and must b=
e
preserved permanently. Deleting or force-pushing it would make those commit=
s
unreachable. `git log`/`git blame` for Rust files resolve against `main-rs`=
,
not `main`.

Versioning splits by engine: C stays at &lt;=3D 5.x from `master`'s version
branches, the Rust engine releases 6.0 and later from version branches cut
off this one. Rolling images stay distinct throughout -- `:edge` from
