numbers for this commit are not reported =E2=80=94 the harness's idle-rate
calibration moved 400x mid-session and alternate runs returned zeros, so
nothing measured after that window is trustworthy. Re-measure on a quiet ho=
st.

* Fuse only the fixed-length traverses; the walks own their predicate

Build-phase fusion cost 1.23x on `vlt edge prop filter` and ~8% on plain
var-length traversals, while every fixed-length traverse stayed flat. The
cost landed entirely on the walks =E2=80=94 which are exactly the two opera=
tors
where the predicate was never a filter on the operator's output.

So the two cases are separated, and the measurement is what confirmed the
distinction rather than motivating a workaround:

`CondTraverse` and `ExpandInto` keep the new arrangement. Their edge is a
single edge bound per row, so a `Filter` above is semantically equivalent a=
