The profile reply hid `Commit` as an &quot;internal implementation detail&q=
uot;,
while `GRAPH.EXPLAIN` has always shown it. `IR::Commit` builds a `CommitOp`
and runs, so hiding it misreports what executed and left the two commands
describing the same plan differently.

The rule is whether the operator exists at runtime, not whether it is
interesting: a `Filter` folded whole into the traverse below it builds no
operator and stays hidden; `Commit` does, so it is listed.

test_profile asserted the root op was Create/Update for write queries; it
