* build(docker): run redis-server as the falkordb user

run.sh starts as root, hands the data directory and the certificates
gen-certs.sh generates to the falkordb user (uid/gid 999), and execs
redis-server through gosu. It stays root when started with --user,
without CAP_SETUID/CAP_SETGID, or with SKIP_DROP_PRIVS=3D1; SKIP_FIX_PERMS=
=3D1
skips the ownership step. The data directory is handed over only when it
holds nothing but *.rdb, nodes*.conf and appendonlydir. New files are
created with umask 0077.

The image creates the falkordb account in place of the redis one at the
same uid/gid, installs gosu in the server stage, and owns the data and TLS
directories as root:falkordb 0775. The ASAN and coverage images set
SKIP_DROP_PRIVS=3D1. The flow-test harness makes the log and temp
directories it creates for spawned containers writable by that user.

Closes #3180

* build(docker): keep redis-server as root when the handover fails

When fix_data_dir_perms leaves the data directory alone (an unrecognised
entry) or a chown fails, and when a generated TLS file cannot be handed
over, run.sh now logs a notice and runs redis-server as root instead of
switching to falkordb. SKIP_FIX_PERMS=3D1 still runs it as falkordb.

Also fixes the stale `gosu redis` in the exec-prefix comment.

