x=3D"true" title=3D"ci: make PR CI fork-safe and gate main on a merge queue=
 (#2718)

* ci: extract the image-dependent half of PR CI into _ci-pipeline.yml

Pure relocation, no behaviour change. The eight jobs that need a published
rc-pr-&lt;N&gt; image =E2=80=94 the three RC builds, `test` against the rel=
ease image,
flow-test-matrix, and the three flow flavours =E2=80=94 move verbatim into =
a
reusable workflow behind three inputs: pr_number, commit_sha, build_image.

rust-pr.yml keeps check-files, docker, lint, coverage and fuzz, and calls
the extracted workflow with exactly the values the jobs read before.

The point is a single definition. A second caller follows in this branch,
and fork CI cannot drift from trunk CI if there is only one copy of the
pipeline to drift.

Substitutions applied to the moved bodies:
  github.event.pull_request.number   -&gt; inputs.pr_number
  github.event.pull_request.head.sha -&gt; inputs.commit_sha
  the file_changed toolchain ternary -&gt; inputs.build_image

and the `needs: [check-files, docker]` gating drops out, since the caller
now owns it.

actionlint findings are conserved exactly across the move: 2x SC2006,
3x SC2046, 6x SC2086, 1x SC2162 before and after, all pre-existing.

* ci: stop re-testing an already-tested tree after merge

Deletes lint, test, build-release, test-flow and fuzz from rust-push.yml.

These run on push to a trunk, against the same tree the PR just tested, and
gate nothing =E2=80=94 the code is already merged by the time they report. =
Measured
on run 33480321390 they are 248 of that workflow's 505 runner-minutes, most
of it test-flow's 117 cells.

Justified by the merge_group gate added later in this branch: once every
commit reaching a trunk has been tested as the merge candidate, a post-merg=
e
re-run is duplicated work rather than a safety net.

Left in place for now, and removed in a follow-up once the queue has proven
the merge-group SHA is the SHA that lands:
  - coverage / build-coverage / coverage-flow, which supply main's Codecov
    baseline. That baseline moves to the queue run, which uploads against
    the commit SHA =E2=80=94 so it only works if that SHA is main's.
  - find-pr, for the same reason: it exists to resolve a commit back to a
    PR number because squash merges produced SHAs that were never built.

No dangling `needs:` remain; flow-test-matrix stays because coverage-flow
still consumes it.

* ci: add an image-free tier to PR CI

Adds build-release, test, flow, build-coverage and coverage-flow to
rust-pr.yml. Each builds libfalkordb.so in the toolchain container, ships i=
t
as a job artifact, and tests against it =E2=80=94 no image is built and not=
hing is
pushed to a registry.

That is the whole point. A pull_request raised from a fork gets a read-only
GITHUB_TOKEN, so `docker push` of the rc-pr-&lt;N&gt; tag is denied and eve=
ry job
consuming that tag skips. These jobs need no registry write at all, so they
run for a fork exactly as they do for a branch. The toolchain container the=
y
start in, ghcr.io/falkordb/falkordb-build:latest, is a public package =E2=
=80=94 an
unauthenticated GHCR manifest request returns 200 =E2=80=94 so no credentia=
l is
needed even to pull it.

Shapes are lifted from the rust-push.yml jobs deleted in the previous
commit, which have been running this way on every push to a trunk. The
coverage variant is simpler here than the image-based one: the module runs
in-process on the runner, so profraws land in the workspace and the
docker-cp-out-of-the-container dance is not needed.

Two structural changes come with it:

  - flow-test-matrix moves back from _ci-pipeline.yml into rust-pr.yml and =
is
    passed down as services_files / spawn_files inputs. Both tiers split th=
e
    same file list, so there is one definition rather than two.

  - _ci-pipeline.yml's `test` becomes `test-image`, so the image-based job
    and the image-free one are distinguishable in the checks list.

The coverage-flow upload is flagged `flow-coverage`. Only unit-tests and fu=
zz
carried a flag before, which is why main's 59% unit-tests figure and its 88=
%
full report could not be attributed to a suite.

* ci: gate on the merge queue, and resolve the toolchain tag once

The new logic in this branch. Five things, all in rust-pr.yml and its calle=
e.

merge_group trigger. A queue entry runs on gh-readonly-queue/&lt;base&gt;/p=
r-N-&lt;sha&gt;,
a branch in this repo, so the token is the base repo's and packages: write =
is
available =E2=80=94 including for a pull request from a fork, with no
pull_request_target anywhere. The queue also tests the merge candidate, so =
what
is tested is what lands.

Concurrency keyed on github.ref. The old key was the PR number, which is em=
pty
under merge_group: every entry would have collapsed into one group and
cancelled its predecessor, which then reports no conclusion and hangs the q=
ueue
until check_response_timeout_minutes. github.ref is documented and non-empt=
y
for both events. cancel-in-progress is off in the queue for the same reason=
.

One toolchain_tag output. The file_changed ternary appeared at eleven call
sites; it is now resolved once in check-files and read everywhere. A missed
call site fails closed in the ugliest way =E2=80=94 a PR that mostly works.

One ci_key output. pr-&lt;N&gt; on a pull request, mg-&lt;sha&gt; in the qu=
eue. Runtime
images are rc-&lt;ci_key&gt;, so a PR still produces exactly rc-pr-&lt;N&gt=
; and nothing
downstream changes yet.

Fork infrastructure changes are refused. Building a fork's Dockerfile needs
packages: write and writes a buildcache ref shared with main's own toolchai=
n
builds. Of the fork PRs this repo has received against a trunk, none has ev=
er
touched build/ or .github/ =E2=80=94 so refusing costs nothing measurable a=
nd removes
the path entirely. The error names the paths and the two remedies; a silent
fallback to :latest would produce errors that look nothing like their cause=
.

Also here:

  - The branches: filter is gone. A PR based on another feature branch neve=
r
    matched it, so stacked PRs got no engine CI at all =E2=80=94 #2693 has =
one check
    run, #2691 four, #2527 eleven, none of them engine tests. Nothing in th=
e
    image-free tier needs a registry write, so there is no reason to withho=
ld
    it from them.

  - ci-gate, the single aggregate check to require. A required check must b=
e
    reported by both events or the merge fails on a status that never arriv=
es,
    and the two tiers deliberately run different jobs.

  - rc-pipeline gains run_flow. In the queue it is the authoritative gate. =
On a
    pull request it publishes the images so release-image.yml can still ret=
ag
    one, but does not re-run suites the image-free tier already ran. Droppi=
ng
    the pull_request half is a follow-up, gated on re-keying release-image.=
yml
    off the commit SHA.

* ci: drop the image-based coverage path, superseded by the artifact one

The image-free tier added earlier in this branch already runs the coverage
flow matrix against a locally built instrumented .so, so build-rc-coverage-=
image
and the image-based flow-coverage were doing the same work twice =E2=80=94 =
once per
push in the image-free tier, once per queue entry through the image.

Deleting the image path is the cheaper half to lose. Nothing ships the cove=
rage
image; it is a pure test rig, so there is no fidelity argument for building=
 it.
And the artifact path is simpler: the module runs in-process on the runner,=
 so
profraws land in the workspace and the collection step does not have to sto=
p
service containers, docker cp their profile directories out, and docker cre=
ate
a throwaway container to extract the module for llvm-cov.

Main's Codecov baseline is unaffected. rust-pr.yml answers to merge_group a=
s of
the previous commit, so the image-free coverage-flow runs on the queue entr=
y too
and uploads against that commit's SHA =E2=80=94 which is the SHA that lands=
 on main.

build/runtime/Dockerfile.coverage is now unreferenced. Left in the tree rat=
her
than deleted in a CI commit; removing it is a separate cleanup.

Deferred: the same conversion for a-sanitizer. It is feasible =E2=80=94 Doc=
kerfile.asan
builds an ASAN redis-server in its own stage, so `docker build --target
redis-asan --output type=3Dlocal` yields the binary without an image push, =
and
RLTest already takes --oss-redis-path. But asan needs three artifacts rathe=
r
than one (module, redis-server, suppressions), it stays in the queue tier
either way so nothing structural depends on it, and unlike everything else =
in
this branch it is new code rather than a rearrangement of job bodies that h=
ave
been running for months. It wants its own PR and a real CI run.

* ci: harden the paths that run pull-request code

persist-credentials: false on both _flow-flavour.yml checkouts. The action
defaults it to true, which writes the token into .git/config =E2=80=94 and =
the next
step runs ./flow.sh, which is test code from the pull request, in that same
workspace. Today a fork's pull_request run holds a read-only token so littl=
e
leaks; a merge_group run executes on a base-repository branch, so the
persisted credential is the base repo's. This is the one change in the bran=
ch
that must land before the queue is switched on, and it is not covered by
refusing fork infrastructure changes: that exclusion deliberately leaves
tests/ open, because a contributor has to be able to add a test.

Buildcache writes only from a trunk. build-toolchain.yml and _build-flavour=
.yml
both cache-to a registry ref that main's own builds restore from. Reading i=
t
from anywhere is fine and keeps builds fast; writing it from a PR branch or=
 a
queue entry is not. cache-from is unchanged.

flow-test-matrix fails over 256 cells. GitHub caps a workflow run's matrix =
at
256 jobs and drops the excess SILENTLY =E2=80=94 the ceiling arrives as tes=
ts quietly
ceasing to run, not as a red X, which is a bad thing to gate a merge queue =
on.
The release flavour is the binding case at 234 cells today (108 services + =
9
spawn, x2 archs): 22 cells of headroom, and the list gained an entry as
recently as 2026-08-27. Also corrects the &quot;97 services-bucket files&qu=
ot; figure in
_flow-flavour.yml's header, which is now 108.

Sweep patterns cover both key shapes. cleanup-rc-images.yml keeps only vers=
ions
where EVERY tag matches its pattern =E2=80=94 a deliberate safety net so a =
promoted
image carrying :edge-rs survives. That makes an unmatched tag shape worse t=
han
a leak: it switches the sweep off for that version entirely. rc-pr-&lt;N&gt=
; becomes
^rc- and the toolchain ^(pr|mg)- so mg-&lt;sha&gt; tags are swept too.

secrets: inherit is gone. Nothing reachable from _ci-pipeline.yml reads a
secret now that the coverage flavour is artifact-based =E2=80=94 _build-fla=
vour only
needs the Docker Hub pair when pushing there, which PR builds do not, and
_flow-flavour only needs CODECOV_TOKEN when collecting coverage. The
image-free coverage jobs have the token directly.

CODEOWNERS for /build/, /.github/ and /tests/ =E2=80=94 the paths that exec=
ute rather
than merely being tested. Fork PRs are refused outright for the first two, =
so
this covers same-repo changes.

Also: the last unflagged Codecov upload gets flags: e2e-tck, and the dead
