x=3D"true" title=3D"feat(index): native numeric index =E2=80=94 CoW columns=
, folded-roots MVCC, read/write paths (#2350)

* feat(index): add index-falkordb feature flag, deps, and EntityType derive=
s

Gate the native numeric index behind the `index-falkordb` Cargo feature (of=
f by default; dark-launched alongside RediSearch). Add Copy + Hash to Entit=
yType so it can key node/edge column maps and the in-flight build set.

(cherry picked from commit 62b658ffd22ed26816568b53ce28962eec7a3291)

* feat(index): order-preserving f64 numeric key encoder

Value -&gt; monotone u64 encoding (sortable), skipping non-numeric/NaN. Boo=
l and temporal map to f64 (parity note tracked separately).

(cherry picked from commit 1e524aa0e5041bcf08767c87d4a679b4f9cc4983)

* feat(index): NumericIndex over the CoW B-tree + RangeIter

Tuple-keyed (encoded_value, doc) index with batched add/remove, bulk from_e=
ntries, and Equal/Range query dispatch yielding doc ids.

(cherry picked from commit 50c247c86a105cf08c33f62b16748e3c4b2879f3)

* feat(index): FalkorDbIndex facade + write maintenance + numeric read rout=
ing

One CoW column per indexed (label, attr), in separate node and edge maps: a
node label and a relationship type can share a name, so a single keyspace
would collide. Cloning is O(1) per column (a root-Arc bump), so the whole
index rides Graph::new_version() and shares pages with the prior version un=
til
a writer touches that column =E2=80=94 folded-roots MVCC, with no separate =
index
versioning. `merge` applies a commit's staged adds and removes in one batch=
ed
pass per column, removes before adds so a (value, id) removed and re-added =
in
the same commit nets to present.

CREATE INDEX on a Range index builds the native column synchronously, on th=
e
write thread, so the create returns with a column that already serves reads=
.
Write maintenance stages (value, id) pairs per column during a commit and
applies them through `merge`, for nodes and edges alike; the delete hooks
stage their removes before the type matrix is torn down, so an edge's type =
is
still resolvable when its removal is recorded. Reads route a numeric
Equal/Range predicate to the native column and fall back to RediSearch for
everything else =E2=80=94 a Range index also holds strings and geo, which R=
