* fix: parse module-load arguments like C, in one place (#3268)

Turn off redismodule-rs's module_args_as_configuration and parse every
load argument pair in graph_init, the way C's Config_Init does: names are
case-insensitive, run-time configs go through the same validation and
setter as GRAPH.CONFIG SET, load-only configs (CACHE_SIZE, THREAD_COUNT,
OMP_THREAD_COUNT, NODE_CREATION_BUFFER, INDEX_WORKER_THREADS,
IMPORT_FOLDER, TEMP_FOLDER) get C's load-time rules, and an invalid value,
an unknown name or an odd argument count refuses the load with C's log
message. C configs this engine does not act on (ASYNC_DELETE,
DELAY_INDEXING, DELTA_MAX_PENDING_CHANGES, EFFECTS_THRESHOLD) are accepted
and logged as deprecated.

Module arguments are now applied after redis.conf's graph.* configs, so
they win over them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;

* refactor: move module-arg parsing to config, validate every pair before a=
pplying

Address review on #3328:
- apply_module_args and its load-only validators live in src/config.rs;
  config_cmd.rs keeps GRAPH.CONFIG and shares its validators/setter.
- Load-only values parse with str::parse::&lt;i64&gt; + is_positive/is_nega=
tive
  (C's strtoll accepts '-0' and rejects &gt;=3D 2^63, so u64/NonZero parses=
 differ).
- Each load-only config maps to its own LoadArg variant; applying is an
  exhaustive match with no wildcard.
- All pairs are validated first (name, value, timeout cross-constraints
  checked in order against a running TIMEOUT_DEFAULT/TIMEOUT_MAX, and the
  TIMEOUT vs TIMEOUT_DEFAULT/MAX conflict), then applied; a refused load
  leaves no partial configuration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;

